<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-17780] Update Kubernetes Deployment examples to StatefulSet</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-17780</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;StatefulSet has been supported since &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6241&quot; title=&quot;Integrate with Kubernetes StatefulSet to support Ignite Persistence&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6241&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6241&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Experience supporting Ignite in the field has led best practice recommendations to stop recommending the use of Kubernetes Deployment objects because of the benefits, in practice, which persistent volumes bring to common operations like restarting pods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Persistent topology and node identity makes re-joining a cluster much cheaper than always creating new Ignite nodes as pods are started.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This should be simple for the cloud provider specific examples: just change the &quot;Creating a Pod Configuration&quot; sections to provide a valid StatefulSet example.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/amazon-eks-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/amazon-eks-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/azure-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/azure-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/gke-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ignite.apache.org/docs/2.11.1/installation/kubernetes/gke-deployment#creating-pod-configuration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
